    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86471" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προᾰκούω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hear beforehand,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.86
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐνυπνίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					10.5.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					22.35
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προακηκόεε ὅτι . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.79
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προακηκοότες ὡς εἶχε</span> how
			matters stood, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.16
			</span></i>; of a horse, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ὠσὶ προακούοντα σημαίνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					4.3.21
				</span></i>
			.</div>
